IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- ss 257 to 260: sale documents deemed prospectuses, application moneys, listing, minimum subscription. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Answers of other functions are passed in as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs; for an exemption only JUST TRUE counts.
-- The exemption of Subdivision (4) in s 257(1)(b) is the answer of another part of the Act and is an input here.
-- A duty is answered as "has the person done what the text requires" (fork F18); a limitation as in s 254(5) (JUST FALSE inside the period, JUST TRUE after).

-- inert (reason 1), lines 41377-41378: s 257 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 41454-41455: s 258 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 41485-41487: s 259 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 41671-41671: s 260 marginal heading: not operative.

§ `s 257: a document offering securities for sale is deemed a prospectus`

-- s 257(1): when subsection (2) applies. "Subsection (2) applies where" is a "where" gate (rule (b)); (b) takes the answer of the Subdivision (4) exemption as an input and only a JUST TRUE exemption defeats it.
-- src:41380 | 257.—(1) Subsection (2) applies where —
-- src:41382 | (a) an entity allots or agrees to allot to any person any
-- src:41383 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of the
-- src:41384 | entity or a business trust (as the case may be) with a view to
-- src:41385 | all or any of them being subsequently offered for sale to
-- src:41386 | another person; and
-- src:41388 | (b) such offer (called in this section a subsequent offer) does
-- src:41389 | not qualify for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of this
-- src:41390 | Division (other than section 280).
@ref s 257(1) (src:41380-41390)
GIVEN
    `an entity allots or agrees to allot securities or contracts with a view to their being subsequently offered for sale to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an entity allot, or agree to allot, to any person any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the entity or a business trust with a view to all or any of them being subsequently offered for sale to another person?
    `the offer qualifies for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13, other than section 280` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the exemption under Subdivision (4) of this Division (other than section 280) answer for the subsequent offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F54 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an entity allots or agrees to allot securities or contracts with a view to their being subsequently offered for sale to another person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where"
        IF (`the offer qualifies for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13, other than section 280` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not qualify for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of this Division (other than section 280)"
        IF (`the offer qualifies for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13, other than section 280` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer for the exemption was not worked out

-- s 257(2): three deemings and a saving. Each deeming applies when subsection (2) applies and the document is the one by which the subsequent offer is made.
-- src:41394 | (2) Any document by which the subsequent offer is made is for all
-- src:41395 | purposes deemed to be a prospectus issued by the entity, and the
-- src:41396 | entity is for all purposes deemed to be the person making the offer,
-- src:41397 | and all written laws and rules of law as to the contents of prospectuses
-- src:41398 | and to liability in respect of statements and non‑disclosure in
-- src:41399 | prospectuses, or otherwise relating to prospectuses, apply and have
-- src:41400 | effect accordingly as if —
-- src:41402 | (a) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:41403 | contracts has been made; and
-- src:41405 | (b) persons accepting the subsequent offer in respect of any
-- src:41406 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts were
-- src:41407 | subscribers therefor,
-- src:41409 | but without affecting the liability (if any) of the persons making the
-- src:41410 | subsequent offer, in respect of statements or non‑disclosures in the
-- src:41411 | document or otherwise.
@ref s 257(2) (src:41394-41411)
GIVEN
    `what section 257(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 257(1) subsection (2) applies` answer for the subsequent offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the document is the one by which the subsequent offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the one by which the subsequent offer is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F55 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(2) the document is deemed to be a prospectus issued by the entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where"
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the document is the one by which the subsequent offer is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any document by which the subsequent offer is made is for all purposes deemed to be a prospectus issued by the entity"

