    `the document is the one by which the subsequent offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the one by which the subsequent offer is made (so that the entity is the person to be deemed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F55 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(2) the entity is deemed to be the person making the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where"
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the document is the one by which the subsequent offer is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the entity is for all purposes deemed to be the person making the offer"

-- src:41394 | (2) Any document by which the subsequent offer is made is for all
-- src:41395 | purposes deemed to be a prospectus issued by the entity, and the
-- src:41396 | entity is for all purposes deemed to be the person making the offer,
-- src:41397 | and all written laws and rules of law as to the contents of prospectuses
-- src:41398 | and to liability in respect of statements and non‑disclosure in
