        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where"
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the document is the one by which the subsequent offer is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "persons accepting the subsequent offer in respect of any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts were subscribers therefor"

@ref s 257(2) (the saving) (src:41394-41411)
GIVEN
    `the liability is that of a person making the subsequent offer in respect of statements or non-disclosures in the document or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one of the persons making the subsequent offer, in respect of statements or non-disclosures in the document or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F55 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(2) the deeming affects the liability of the persons making the subsequent offer` MEANS
    IF `the liability is that of a person making the subsequent offer in respect of statements or non-disclosures in the document or otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but without affecting the liability (if any) of the persons making the subsequent offer, in respect of statements or non-disclosures in the document or otherwise"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the liability (if any) of the persons making the subsequent offer" says nothing of any other liability

-- s 257(3): evidence. "unless the contrary is proved" is a closed gate. (a) an offer for sale made within 6 months after the allotment; or (b) the whole consideration not yet received at the date of the offer.
-- src:41418 | (3) For the purposes of this Act, unless the contrary is proved, it is
-- src:41419 | sufficient evidence that an allotment of, or an agreement to allot,
-- src:41420 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts was made with a
-- src:41421 | view to the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts being
-- src:41422 | subsequently offered for sale if it is shown —
-- src:41424 | (a) that an offer of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:41425 | derivatives contracts or of any of them for sale was
-- src:41426 | made within 6 months after the allotment or agreement to
-- src:41427 | allot; or
-- src:41429 | (b) that at the date when the offer was made the whole
-- src:41430 | consideration to be received by the entity in respect of the
-- src:41431 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts had not
-- src:41432 | been so received.
@ref s 257(3) (src:41418-41432)
GIVEN
    `the date of the allotment or the agreement to allot` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the allotment, or the agreement to allot, made?
    `the date the offer for sale was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the offer for sale made?
    `the whole consideration to be received by the entity had not been received at the date of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the date when the offer was made, had the whole consideration to be received by the entity in respect of the securities or contracts not yet been received?
    `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contrary proved (that the allotment was not made with a view to the securities being subsequently offered for sale)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F56 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(3) it is sufficient evidence that the allotment was made with a view to subsequent sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contrary is proved`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the contrary is proved, it is sufficient evidence"
        IF (`the date the offer for sale was made` AT LEAST `the date of the allotment or the agreement to allot` AND `the date the offer for sale was made` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the allotment or the agreement to allot` 6 Months)) OR `the whole consideration to be received by the entity had not been received at the date of the offer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is sufficient evidence ... if it is shown" names two ways and says nothing of any other

-- src:41436 | (4) The requirements of this Division as to prospectuses have effect
-- src:41437 | as though the persons making the subsequent offer were persons
-- src:41438 | named in the prospectus as directors or equivalent persons of the
-- src:41439 | entity.
@ref s 257(4) (src:41436-41439)
GIVEN
    `what section 257(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 257(1) subsection (2) applies` answer for the subsequent offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person makes the subsequent offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the subsequent offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F55 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(4) the person making the subsequent offer is treated as a person named in the prospectus as a director` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where"
        IF (`what section 257(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person makes the subsequent offer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as though the persons making the subsequent offer were persons named in the prospectus as directors or equivalent persons of the entity"

-- src:41441 | (5) In addition to complying with the other requirements of this
-- src:41442 | Division, the document making the subsequent offer must state —
-- src:41444 | (a) the net amount of the consideration received or to be
-- src:41445 | received by the entity in respect of the securities or
-- src:41446 | securities‑based derivatives contracts being offered; and
-- src:41448 | (b) the place and time at which a copy of the contract under
-- src:41449 | which the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:41450 | contracts have been or are to be allotted may be inspected.
@ref s 257(5) (src:41441-41450)
GIVEN
    `the document makes the subsequent offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the one making the subsequent offer?
    `the document states the net amount of the consideration received or to be received by the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state the net amount of the consideration received or to be received by the entity in respect of the securities or contracts being offered?
    `the document states the place and time at which a copy of the contract may be inspected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document state the place and time at which a copy of the contract under which the securities or contracts have been or are to be allotted may be inspected?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F18 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 257(5) the document states what it must state` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document makes the subsequent offer`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the document making the subsequent offer must state"
        IF `the document states the net amount of the consideration received or to be received by the entity` AND `the document states the place and time at which a copy of the contract may be inspected`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state"

§ `s 258: application moneys held in trust in a separate bank account until allotment`

-- s 258(1): the duty to hold. The duty runs "until the allotment", so after the allotment it is no longer shown to arise (NOTHING, fork F18); money that is not application money paid before allotment is outside the scope (NOTHING).
-- src:41457 | 258.—(1) All application and other moneys paid prior to allotment
-- src:41458 | by any applicant on account of securities or securities‑based
-- src:41459 | derivatives contracts offered to the applicant must, until the
-- src:41460 | allotment of the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts,
-- src:41461 | be held by the person making the offer of the securities or
-- src:41462 | securities‑based derivatives contracts upon trust for the applicant in
-- src:41467 | a separate bank account, being a bank account that is established and
-- src:41468 | kept by the person solely for the purpose of depositing the application
-- src:41469 | and other moneys that are paid by applicants for those securities or
-- src:41470 | securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 258(1) (src:41457-41470)
GIVEN
    `the moneys are application or other moneys paid prior to allotment by an applicant on account of securities or contracts offered to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the moneys application or other moneys paid, prior to allotment, by an applicant on account of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered to the applicant?
    `the allotment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the allotment of the securities or contracts been made?
    `the person making the offer holds the moneys upon trust for the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person making the offer hold the moneys upon trust for the applicant?
    `the moneys are in a separate bank account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the moneys in a separate bank account?
    `the bank account is established and kept by the person solely for depositing the application and other moneys paid by applicants for those securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the bank account one established and kept by the person solely for the purpose of depositing the application and other moneys paid by applicants for those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F18 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 258(1) the person making the offer holds the moneys on trust in a separate bank account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the moneys are application or other moneys paid prior to allotment by an applicant on account of securities or contracts offered to the applicant`) OR `the allotment has been made`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All application and other moneys paid prior to allotment by any applicant on account of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered to the applicant must, until the allotment"
        IF `the person making the offer holds the moneys upon trust for the applicant` AND `the moneys are in a separate bank account` AND `the bank account is established and kept by the person solely for depositing the application and other moneys paid by applicants for those securities or contracts`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be held by the person making the offer of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts upon trust for the applicant in a separate bank account"

-- src:41474 | (2) There is no obligation or duty on any bank with which any such
-- src:41475 | moneys have been deposited to enquire into or see to the proper
-- src:41476 | application of those moneys, so long as the bank acts in good faith.
@ref s 258(2) (src:41474-41476)
GIVEN
    `the bank acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the bank act in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F57 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 258(2) the bank has an obligation or duty to enquire into the application of the moneys` MEANS
    IF `the bank acts in good faith`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There is no obligation or duty on any bank with which any such moneys have been deposited to enquire into or see to the proper application of those moneys, so long as the bank acts in good faith"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so long as the bank acts in good faith" says no duty while the bank acts in good faith and says nothing of a bank that does not

-- src:41478 | (3) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:41479 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:41480 | $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:41481 | both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:41482 | exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:41483 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 258(3) (src:41478-41483)
GIVEN
    `what section 258(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 258(1) the person making the offer holds the moneys on trust in a separate bank account` answer for the person making the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F58 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 258(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `what section 258(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 258(3) (the penalty) (src:41478-41483)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 258(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 24, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

§ `s 259: allotment where the prospectus indicates an application to list`

DECLARE `s 259 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 259(11) issue the prospectus inviting persons to subscribe`

-- s 259(1)(a): the application in the form required within 3 days from the date of the issue. The "Where" block of the chapeau is a gate (rule (b)).
-- src:41489 | 259.—(1) Where a prospectus states or implies that application has
-- src:41490 | been or will be made for permission for the securities or
-- src:41491 | securities‑based derivatives contracts offered thereby to be listed
-- src:41492 | for quotation on any approved exchange, and —
-- src:41494 | (a) the permission is not applied for in the form required by the
-- src:41495 | approved exchange within 3 days from the date of the issue
-- src:41496 | of the prospectus; or
@ref s 259(1)(a) (src:41489-41496)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made for permission to list the securities or contracts for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus state or imply that application has been or will be made for permission for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered by it to be listed for quotation on any approved exchange?
    `the date of the issue of the prospectus` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus issued?
    `permission was applied for in the form required by the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was permission applied for in the form required by the approved exchange?
    `the date permission was applied for` IS A DATE @desc On what date was permission applied for in the form required (any date if it was not applied for)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F59 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(1)(a) the permission was not applied for in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made for permission to list the securities or contracts for quotation on an approved exchange`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made for permission for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered thereby to be listed for quotation on any approved exchange"
        IF (NOT `permission was applied for in the form required by the approved exchange`) OR (NOT (`the date permission was applied for` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the issue of the prospectus` 3 Days)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the permission is not applied for in the form required by the approved exchange within 3 days from the date of the issue of the prospectus"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 259(1)(b): permission not granted before the expiration of 6 weeks from the date of the issue, or of such longer period not exceeding 12 weeks as is, within those 6 weeks, notified. A notified period outside 7 to 12 weeks is not one the text allows, so 6 weeks stands (fork F59).
-- src:41489 | 259.—(1) Where a prospectus states or implies that application has
-- src:41490 | been or will be made for permission for the securities or
-- src:41491 | securities‑based derivatives contracts offered thereby to be listed
-- src:41492 | for quotation on any approved exchange, and —
-- src:41494 | (a) the permission is not applied for in the form required by the
-- src:41495 | approved exchange within 3 days from the date of the issue
-- src:41496 | of the prospectus; or
-- src:41498 | (b) the permission is not granted before the expiration of
-- src:41499 | 6 weeks from the date of the issue of the prospectus or such
-- src:41500 | longer period not exceeding 12 weeks from the date of the
-- src:41501 | issue as is, within those 6 weeks, notified to the applicant
-- src:41502 | by or on behalf of the approved exchange,
@ref s 259(1)(b) (src:41489-41502)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made for permission to list the securities or contracts for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus state or imply that application has been or will be made for permission for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered by it to be listed for quotation on any approved exchange?
    `the date of the issue of the prospectus` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus issued?
    `permission was granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was permission granted?
    `the date permission was granted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was permission granted (any date if it was not granted)?
    `the number of weeks of a longer period notified within the 6 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks is the longer period that the approved exchange, or someone for it, notified to the applicant within the 6 weeks (0 if none was notified)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F59 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(1)(b) the permission was not granted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made for permission to list the securities or contracts for quotation on an approved exchange`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made for permission for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered thereby to be listed for quotation on any approved exchange"
        IF (NOT `permission was granted`) OR (NOT (`the date permission was granted` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the issue of the prospectus` (IF (`the number of weeks of a longer period notified within the 6 weeks` GREATER THAN 6) AND (`the number of weeks of a longer period notified within the 6 weeks` AT MOST 12) THEN `the number of weeks of a longer period notified within the 6 weeks` ELSE 6) Weeks)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the permission is not granted before the expiration of 6 weeks from the date of the issue of the prospectus or such longer period not exceeding 12 weeks"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

@ref s 259(1) (the trigger) (src:41489-41502)
GIVEN
    `what section 259(1)(a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(1)(a) the permission was not applied for in time` answer for the prospectus? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 259(1)(b) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(1)(b) the permission was not granted in time` answer for the prospectus? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
