-- FORK F59 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(1) the permission was not applied for or not granted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 259(1)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 259(1)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 259(1)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 259(1)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the permission is not applied for in the form required by the approved exchange within 3 days"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under paragraph (a) or (b) was not worked out

-- s 259(1)(c): the allotment is void, subject to subsection (3). The exemption is passed in as an answer; only JUST TRUE counts.
-- src:41504 | then —
-- src:41506 | (c) any allotment whenever made of securities or
-- src:41507 | securities‑based derivatives contracts made on an
-- src:41508 | application pursuant to the prospectus is, subject to
-- src:41509 | subsection (3), void; and
@ref s 259(1)(c) (src:41504-41509)
GIVEN
    `what section 259(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(1) the permission was not applied for or not granted in time` answer for the prospectus? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the allotment was made on an application pursuant to the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the allotment made on an application pursuant to the prospectus?
    `what section 259(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(3) the Authority may exempt the allotment` answer for the allotment? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F60 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(1)(c) the allotment is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then"
        IF (`what section 259(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, subject to subsection (3), void"
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the allotment was made on an application pursuant to the prospectus`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any allotment whenever made of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made on an application pursuant to the prospectus"

-- s 259(1)(d): the offence of continuing to allot after the period. The last day of the period is an input (the last day of the period of paragraph (a) or (b) that was missed).
-- src:41514 | (d) any person who continues to allot such securities or
-- src:41515 | securities‑based derivatives contracts after the period
-- src:41516 | specified in paragraph (a) or (b), shall be guilty of an
-- src:41517 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:41518 | exceeding $150,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:41519 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:41520 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every
-- src:41521 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:41522 | after conviction.
@ref s 259(1)(d) (src:41514-41522)
GIVEN
    `what section 259(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(1) the permission was not applied for or not granted in time` answer for the prospectus? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the last day of the period specified in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period specified in section 259(1)(a) or (b) that was missed (3 days from the issue for paragraph (a); 6 weeks, or the longer period, for paragraph (b))?
    `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the person allot?
    `the person continues to allot the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to allot such securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `what section 259(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(3) the Authority may exempt the allotment` answer for the allotment? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F61 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(1)(d) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`what section 259(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made"
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person continues to allot the securities or contracts` AND (NOT (`the date of the allotment` AT MOST `the last day of the period specified in paragraph (a) or (b)`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who continues to allot such securities or securities-based derivatives contracts after the period specified in paragraph (a) or (b)"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer under subsection (1) was not worked out

@ref s 259(1)(d) (the penalty) (src:41514-41522)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 259(1)(d) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 150000, 24, TRUE, 15000  -- a fine not exceeding $150,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years, or both; a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 259(2): repayment. The duty arises "where the permission has not been applied for, or has not been granted as mentioned under subsection (1)". It is subject to subsection (3).
-- src:41526 | (2) Where the permission has not been applied for, or has not been
-- src:41527 | granted as mentioned under subsection (1), the person making the
-- src:41528 | offer must, subject to subsection (3), immediately repay without
-- src:41529 | interest all moneys received from applicants pursuant to the
-- src:41530 | prospectus, and if any such moneys is not repaid within 14 days
-- src:41531 | after the person making the offer so becomes liable to repay them,
-- src:41532 | then —
@ref s 259(2) (src:41526-41532)
GIVEN
    `what section 259(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(1) the permission was not applied for or not granted in time` answer for the prospectus? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 259(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(3) the Authority may exempt the allotment` answer for the allotment? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person making the offer has immediately repaid, without interest, all moneys received from applicants pursuant to the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer immediately repaid, without interest, all moneys received from applicants pursuant to the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F18 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(2) the person making the offer has repaid the moneys` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the permission has not been applied for, or has not been granted as mentioned under subsection (1), the person making the offer must"
        IF (`what section 259(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (3)"
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person making the offer has immediately repaid, without interest, all moneys received from applicants pursuant to the prospectus`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 259(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, subject to subsection (3), immediately repay without interest all moneys received from applicants pursuant to the prospectus"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer under subsection (1) was not worked out

-- src:41526 | (2) Where the permission has not been applied for, or has not been
-- src:41527 | granted as mentioned under subsection (1), the person making the
-- src:41528 | offer must, subject to subsection (3), immediately repay without
-- src:41529 | interest all moneys received from applicants pursuant to the
-- src:41530 | prospectus, and if any such moneys is not repaid within 14 days
-- src:41531 | after the person making the offer so becomes liable to repay them,
