@ref s 259(10) (the penalty) (src:41616-41621)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 259(10) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 259(11): the bar on issuing a prospectus that refers to listing. "unless" closes (b) when (i) or (ii) is met.
-- src:41623 | (11) A person must not issue a prospectus inviting persons to
-- src:41624 | subscribe for securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of an
-- src:41625 | entity if it includes —
-- src:41627 | (a) a false or misleading statement that permission has been
-- src:41628 | granted for those securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:41629 | contracts to be listed for quotation on, dealt in or quoted on
-- src:41630 | any approved exchange; or
-- src:41632 | (b) any statement in any way referring to any such permission
-- src:41633 | or to any application or intended application for any such
-- src:41634 | permission, or to listing for quotation, dealing in or quoting
-- src:41635 | the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts on
-- src:41636 | any approved exchange, or to any requirement of an
-- src:41637 | approved exchange, unless —
-- src:41639 | (i) that statement is or is to the effect that permission has
-- src:41640 | been granted, or that application has been or will be
-- src:41641 | made to the approved exchange within 3 days after
-- src:41642 | the date of the issue of the prospectus; or
-- src:41644 | (ii) that statement has been approved by the Authority
-- src:41645 | for inclusion in the prospectus.
@ref s 259(11) (src:41623-41645)
GIVEN
    `the person issues a prospectus inviting persons to subscribe for securities or contracts of an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you issue a prospectus inviting persons to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of an entity?
    `the prospectus includes a false or misleading statement that permission has been granted for listing, dealing or quotation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus include a false or misleading statement that permission has been granted for the securities or contracts to be listed for quotation on, dealt in or quoted on any approved exchange?
    `the prospectus includes a statement referring to such permission, an application or intended application, listing, dealing, quoting or a requirement of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus include any statement in any way referring to any such permission or to any application or intended application for it, or to listing for quotation, dealing in or quoting the securities or contracts on any approved exchange, or to any requirement of an approved exchange?
    `the statement is to the effect that permission has been granted, or that application has been or will be made within 3 days after the date of the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement, or is it to the effect, that permission has been granted, or that application has been or will be made to the approved exchange within 3 days after the date of the issue of the prospectus?
    `the statement has been approved by the Authority for inclusion in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority approved the statement for inclusion in the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F67 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(11) the person must not issue the prospectus` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person issues a prospectus inviting persons to subscribe for securities or contracts of an entity`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not issue a prospectus inviting persons to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of an entity"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the prospectus includes a false or misleading statement that permission has been granted for listing, dealing or quotation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the prospectus includes a statement referring to such permission, an application or intended application, listing, dealing, quoting or a requirement of an approved exchange` AND (`the statement is to the effect that permission has been granted, or that application has been or will be made within 3 days after the date of the issue` OR `the statement has been approved by the Authority for inclusion in the prospectus`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless" ... "that statement is or is to the effect that permission has been granted, or that application has been or will be made to the approved exchange within 3 days after the date of the issue of the prospectus" ... "that statement has been approved by the Authority for inclusion in the prospectus"
        IF `the prospectus includes a statement referring to such permission, an application or intended application, listing, dealing, quoting or a requirement of an approved exchange`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it includes" ... "a false or misleading statement that permission has been granted" ... "any statement in any way referring to any such permission"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 259(11) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:41623-41645)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who issues the prospectus?
    `what section 259(11) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(11) the person must not issue the prospectus` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 259 action`
`s 259(11) the person shall not issue the prospectus` MEANS
    IF `what section 259(11) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 259(11) issue the prospectus inviting persons to subscribe`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the prospectus was issued with a false or misleading statement about permission, or a statement about listing that no exception covers; section 259(12) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:41649 | (12) Any person who contravenes subsection (11) shall be guilty of
-- src:41650 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:41651 | $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to
-- src:41652 | both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:41653 | exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:41654 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 259(12) (src:41649-41654)
GIVEN
    `what section 259(11) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 259(11) the person must not issue the prospectus` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F58 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(12) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `what section 259(11) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (11) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 259(12) (the penalty) (src:41649-41654)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 259(12) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- src:41659 | (13) Where a prospectus contains a statement to the effect that the
-- src:41660 | memorandum and articles or other constituent document or
-- src:41661 | documents of the issuer comply, or have been drawn so as to
-- src:41662 | comply, with the requirements of any approved exchange, the
-- src:41663 | prospectus is, unless the contrary intention appears from the
-- src:41664 | prospectus, deemed for the purposes of this section to imply that
-- src:41665 | application has been, or will be, made for permission for the securities
-- src:41666 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus
-- src:41667 | relates to be listed for quotation on the approved exchange.
@ref s 259(13) (src:41659-41667)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus contains a statement that the memorandum and articles or other constituent documents of the issuer comply with the requirements of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus contain a statement to the effect that the memorandum and articles or other constituent document or documents of the issuer comply, or have been drawn so as to comply, with the requirements of any approved exchange?
    `the contrary intention appears from the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contrary intention appear from the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F68 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 259(13) the prospectus is deemed to imply that application has been or will be made for permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus contains a statement that the memorandum and articles or other constituent documents of the issuer comply with the requirements of an approved exchange`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a prospectus contains a statement to the effect that the memorandum and articles or other constituent document or documents of the issuer comply"
        IF `the contrary intention appears from the prospectus`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the contrary intention appears from the prospectus"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 260: no allotment unless the minimum subscription is received`

DECLARE `s 260 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 260(1) make an allotment before the minimum subscription is subscribed and the sums received`

-- src:41686 | (1A) Despite subsection (1), if a cheque for the sum payable
-- src:41687 | mentioned in subsection (1) has been received by the company or the
-- src:41688 | trustee‑manager of the business trust (as the case may be), the sum is
-- src:41689 | treated as not having been received by the company or the
-- src:41690 | trustee‑manager (as the case may be) until the cheque is paid by
-- src:41691 | the bank on which the cheque is drawn.
@ref s 260(1A) (src:41686-41691)
GIVEN
    `the sum payable on application has been received by cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum payable on application been received by cheque by the company or the trustee-manager?
    `the cheque has been paid by the bank on which it is drawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the cheque been paid by the bank on which it is drawn?
    `the sum payable on application has been received otherwise than by cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum payable on application been received otherwise than by cheque?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F69 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(1A) the sum payable on application is treated as received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sum payable on application has been received by cheque` AND (NOT `the cheque has been paid by the bank on which it is drawn`) AND (NOT `the sum payable on application has been received otherwise than by cheque`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the sum is treated as not having been received by the company or the trustee-manager (as the case may be) until the cheque is paid by the bank on which the cheque is drawn"
        IF (`the sum payable on application has been received by cheque` AND `the cheque has been paid by the bank on which it is drawn`) OR `the sum payable on application has been received otherwise than by cheque`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no sum is shown as received

-- src:41673 | 260.—(1) A person must not make an allotment of any securities or
-- src:41674 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of a company or business trust
-- src:41675 | unless —
-- src:41677 | (a) the minimum subscription has been subscribed; and
-- src:41679 | (b) the sum payable on application for the securities or
-- src:41680 | securities‑based derivatives contracts so subscribed has
-- src:41681 | been received by the company or the trustee‑manager, as
-- src:41682 | the case may be.
@ref s 260(1) (src:41673-41682)
GIVEN
    `the person makes an allotment of securities or contracts of a company or business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an allotment of any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a company or business trust?
    `the minimum subscription has been subscribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minimum subscription been subscribed?
    `what section 260(1A) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 260(1A) the sum payable on application is treated as received` answer for the sum payable on application for the securities or contracts so subscribed? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F69 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(1) the person must not make the allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person makes an allotment of securities or contracts of a company or business trust`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not make an allotment of any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a company or business trust"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the minimum subscription has been subscribed` AND (`what section 260(1A) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless" ... "the minimum subscription has been subscribed" ... "the sum payable on application for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts so subscribed has been received"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 260(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:41673-41682)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who makes the allotment?
    `what section 260(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 260(1) the person must not make the allotment` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 260 action`
`s 260(1) the person shall not make the allotment` MEANS
    IF `what section 260(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 260(1) make an allotment before the minimum subscription is subscribed and the sums received`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "an allotment was made before the minimum subscription was subscribed and the sum payable on application received; section 260(7) makes the allotment voidable"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:41695 | (2) The minimum subscription must —
-- src:41697 | (a) be calculated based on the price at which each share or
-- src:41698 | debenture, each unit of share or debenture, or each unit or
-- src:41699 | derivative of a unit in a business trust, is or will be offered;
-- src:41700 | and
-- src:41702 | (b) be reckoned exclusively of any amount payable otherwise
-- src:41703 | than in cash.
@ref s 260(2) (src:41695-41703)
GIVEN
    `the minimum subscription is calculated based on the price at which each security or unit is or will be offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the minimum subscription calculated based on the price at which each share or debenture, each unit of share or debenture, or each unit or derivative of a unit in a business trust, is or will be offered?
    `the minimum subscription is reckoned exclusively of any amount payable otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the minimum subscription reckoned exclusively of any amount payable otherwise than in cash?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F70 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(2) the minimum subscription is calculated as it must be` MEANS
    IF `the minimum subscription is calculated based on the price at which each security or unit is or will be offered` AND `the minimum subscription is reckoned exclusively of any amount payable otherwise than in cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The minimum subscription must" ... "be calculated based on the price at which each share or debenture, each unit of share or debenture, or each unit or derivative of a unit in a business trust, is or will be offered" ... "be reckoned exclusively of any amount payable otherwise than in cash"

-- src:41710 | (3) The amount payable on application on each share or debenture,
-- src:41711 | or each unit of share or debenture, or each unit or derivative of a unit
-- src:41712 | in a business trust, offered must not be less than 5% of the price at
-- src:41713 | which the share or debenture, or unit of share or debenture, or unit or
-- src:41714 | derivative of a unit in a business trust, is or will be offered.
@ref s 260(3) (src:41710-41714)
GIVEN
    `the price at which the share, debenture, unit or derivative is or will be offered` IS A NUMBER @desc At what price, in dollars, is the share, debenture, unit of share or debenture, or unit or derivative of a unit in a business trust, or will it be, offered?
    `the amount payable on application on each` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, is payable on application on each?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F70 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(3) the amount payable on application is not less than 5% of the price` MEANS
    IF `the amount payable on application on each` * 20 AT LEAST `the price at which the share, debenture, unit or derivative is or will be offered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be less than 5% of the price at which the share or debenture, or unit of share or debenture, or unit or derivative of a unit in a business trust, is or will be offered"

-- src:41718 | (4) If the conditions referred to in subsection (1)(a) and (b) have not
-- src:41719 | been satisfied on the expiration of 4 months after the first issue of the
-- src:41720 | prospectus, all moneys received from applicants for securities or
-- src:41721 | securities‑based derivatives contracts must be immediately repaid to
-- src:41722 | them without interest.
@ref s 260(4) (src:41718-41722)
GIVEN
    `the conditions in subsection (1)(a) and (b) were satisfied on the expiration of 4 months after the first issue of the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the conditions in section 260(1)(a) and (b) satisfied on the expiration of 4 months after the first issue of the prospectus?
    `all moneys received from applicants have been immediately repaid without interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all moneys received from applicants been immediately repaid to them without interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F18 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(4) the moneys have been repaid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the conditions in subsection (1)(a) and (b) were satisfied on the expiration of 4 months after the first issue of the prospectus`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the conditions referred to in subsection (1)(a) and (b) have not been satisfied on the expiration of 4 months after the first issue of the prospectus"
        IF `all moneys received from applicants have been immediately repaid without interest`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all moneys received from applicants for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts must be immediately repaid to them without interest"

-- src:41735 | (6) A director is not liable under subsection (5) if the director
-- src:41736 | proves that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to
-- src:41737 | any misconduct or negligence on the part of the director.
@ref s 260(6) (src:41735-41737)
GIVEN
    `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director?
    `the person proves that the default in the repayment was not due to any misconduct or negligence on the person's part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on your part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F53 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(6) this section gives the director a defence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is a director`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director is not liable under subsection (5)"
        IF `the person proves that the default in the repayment was not due to any misconduct or negligence on the person's part`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the director proves that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on the part of the director"

-- src:41726 | (5) If any money mentioned in subsection (4) is not repaid within
-- src:41727 | 5 months after the issue of the prospectus, the directors of the
-- src:41728 | company or the directors of the trustee‑manager of the business trust
-- src:41729 | (as the case may be) are jointly and severally liable to repay that
-- src:41730 | money with interest at the rate of 10% per annum from the expiration
-- src:41731 | of the period of 5 months.
@ref s 260(5) (src:41726-41731)
GIVEN
    `the date of the issue of the prospectus` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus issued?
    `the money has been repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the money mentioned in subsection (4) been repaid?
    `the date the money was repaid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it repaid (any date if not repaid)?
    `the person is a director of the company or of the trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company, or of the trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `what section 260(6) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 260(6) this section gives the director a defence` answer for the director? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F62 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(5) the director is jointly and severally liable to repay with interest at 10% per annum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is a director of the company or of the trustee-manager of the business trust`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the directors of the company or the directors of the trustee-manager of the business trust (as the case may be) are jointly and severally liable"
        IF `the money has been repaid` AND (`the date the money was repaid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the issue of the prospectus` 5 Months))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any money mentioned in subsection (4) is not repaid within 5 months after the issue of the prospectus"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF (`what section 260(6) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director is not liable under subsection (5)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 260(7): the allottee's option to avoid. The option is exercised by written notice within one month: from the statutory meeting, or from the allotment where no statutory meeting is required or the allotment follows it (a window the text fixes in its own words: JUST FALSE outside it).
-- src:41741 | (7) An allotment made by a company or a trustee‑manager of a
-- src:41742 | business trust to an applicant in contravention of this section is
-- src:41743 | voidable at the option of the applicant, which option may be exercised
-- src:41744 | by written notice served —
-- src:41746 | (a) if the allotment is made by a company, on the company —
-- src:41748 | (i) within one month after the holding of the statutory
-- src:41749 | meeting of the company; or
-- src:41751 | (ii) where the company is not required to hold a statutory
-- src:41752 | meeting, or where the allotment is made after the
-- src:41753 | holding of the statutory meeting, within one month
-- src:41754 | after the date of the allotment; or
-- src:41759 | (b) if the allotment is made by a trustee‑manager of a business
-- src:41760 | trust, on the trustee‑manager of the business trust within
-- src:41761 | one month after the date of the allotment.
@ref s 260(7) (src:41741-41761)
GIVEN
    `the allotment is made in contravention of section 260` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment made by a company or a trustee-manager of a business trust to the applicant in contravention of section 260?
    `the allotter is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment made by a company (and not by the trustee-manager of a business trust)?
    `the company is required to hold a statutory meeting and the allotment was made before it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company required to hold a statutory meeting, and was the allotment made before the holding of the statutory meeting?
    `the date of the statutory meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statutory meeting of the company held (any date if none applies)?
    `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the allotment made?
    `the notice is in writing and served on the company or the trustee-manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing, and served on the company (or on the trustee-manager of the business trust)?
    `the date the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice served?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F71 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(7) the applicant has exercised the option to avoid the allotment in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the allotment is made in contravention of section 260`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An allotment made by a company or a trustee-manager of a business trust to an applicant in contravention of this section is voidable"
        IF `the notice is in writing and served on the company or the trustee-manager` AND (`the date the notice was served` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` (IF `the allotter is a company` AND `the company is required to hold a statutory meeting and the allotment was made before it` THEN `the date of the statutory meeting` ELSE `the date of the allotment`) 1 Months))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month after the holding of the statutory meeting of the company" ... "within one month after the date of the allotment"

-- src:41765 | (7A) The allotment mentioned in subsection (7) is voidable even if
-- src:41766 | the company or business trust is in the course of being wound up.
@ref s 260(7A) (src:41765-41766)
GIVEN
    `the allotment is made in contravention of section 260` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment made in contravention of section 260?
    `the company or business trust is in the course of being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the company or business trust in the course of being wound up?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F71 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(7A) the allotment is voidable although the company or business trust is being wound up` MEANS
    IF `the allotment is made in contravention of section 260` AND `the company or business trust is in the course of being wound up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The allotment mentioned in subsection (7) is voidable even if the company or business trust is in the course of being wound up"

-- s 260(7B), (7C), (7D): offences and the money liabilities that go with them. The text states no penalty for these offences (only "the penalty or punishment for the offence"), so there is no penalty function (NOTES, "What the text does not answer").
