`s 260(7B) the trustee-manager is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the trustee-manager of a business trust contravenes a provision of this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A trustee-manager of a business trust which contravenes any of the provisions of this section shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 260(7B)(a) (src:41770-41782)
GIVEN
    `the trustee-manager of a business trust contravenes a provision of this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee-manager of a business trust contravene any of the provisions of section 260?
    `the business trust has sustained loss, damages or costs as a consequence of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the business trust (represented by any diminishment in value to the trust property) sustained or incurred any loss, damages or costs as a consequence of the contravention?
