-- s 260(8): a limitation. "No proceedings ... may be commenced after the expiration of 2 years from the date of the allotment": JUST FALSE inside the period the text fixes, JUST TRUE after it (as at section 254(5)). The text says "compensation under subsection (7)"; compensation is provided in (7B), (7C) and (7D), and the function reads (8) as covering them (fork F73).
-- src:41823 | (8) No proceedings for the recovery of any compensation under
-- src:41824 | subsection (7) may be commenced after the expiration of 2 years from
-- src:41825 | the date of the allotment.
@ref s 260(8) (src:41823-41825)
GIVEN
    `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the allotment made?
    `the date on which the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date are the proceedings for the recovery of compensation commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F73 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 260(8) the proceedings may not be commenced` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the proceedings are commenced` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the allotment` 2 Years)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the expiration of 2 years from the date of the allotment"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

